  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct Assistance and Early Adaptation Support to Persons Affected by the Crisis in Ukraine Living in Bulgaria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following the onset of the full-scale invasion of Ukraine by the Russian Federation on 24 February 2022, there have been unprecedented migratory movements within Ukraine, as well as towards other European countries. With this project, IOM Bulgaria is contributing to strengthening the Bulgarian reception system and responding to the immediate assistance, early adaptation, and integration needs of conflict-affected persons, including Ukrainian asylum seekers and refugees, as well as third country nationals, who have fled Ukraine and are living in Bulgaria. IOM is supporting these groups through the provision by mobile response teams of information and interpretation support, facilitating access to administrative, health care and other services, and initial adaptation, and integration support in Bulgaria through language courses, financial grants, and emergency accommodation.</narrative>
  </description>
